------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <HelpIcon> is a tiny PRESENTATIONAL PRIMITIVE. Its only data source is the SYNCHRONOUS
useTranslation; it takes plain props (i18nKey, content, for, side, ariaLabel) and renders a `(?)` trigger
that reveals a <Tooltip>. There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO loading /
error / stale / offline branch (there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from). Reproducing
those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this surface reproduces only
the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition the sibling presentational primitives Accordion (0203),
MetricCard (0095), InlineCallout (0124), ActiveFilterChips (0147), and StaggerItem (0194) used. The REAL
branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • absent               : no i18nKey + no content (or a string that resolves empty) -> renders NOTHING
                           (web `if (!text) return null`), a deliberate zero-footprint absence so adopting
                           call-sites need not gate the icon themselves — NOT a blank box.
  • resting              : the muted `(?)` trigger; help bubble hidden.
  • presented            : tap (keyboard Return/Space) or macOS pointer hover reveals the help copy; Escape
                           / outside-tap dismiss (web Escape-to-blur).
  • label resolution     : ariaLabel override wins (web nullish ??, even empty); else for -> "Help for
                           {field}" (a11y.helpFor); else generic "More info" (help.tooltip.iconLabel).
  • placement            : per-side bubble (web side; left/right fold to leading/trailing for RTL).
  • reduced motion       : the bubble entrance fades via TSFadeIn; instant under Reduce Motion.
Data source  : useTranslation only (synchronous i18n; no fetch).
Shared comps : none (the web source maps none -> none required).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : a11y.helpFor + help.tooltip.iconLabel (REAL web t() keys, mirrored) resolved through the
               P1/S10 facade; the help text key is caller-owned with content as the defaultValue.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "HelpIcon" (P1/S11) when the trigger renders.
a11y         : trigger is one button with explicit label (web aria-label) + open hint + the help text as its
               VoiceOver hint (the native peer of aria-describedby); glyph hidden from VoiceOver; the bubble
               carries the \(for)-help identifier; Dynamic Type via tokens; reduce-motion honored.

